# Balancing work across teams, with a quadratic objective.
#
# The point of this file is the objective. Every other model in this repository
# measures imbalance as a range — the busiest team minus the idlest — because
# that is the linear measure of the idea. A range is blind to everything in the
# middle: it cannot tell three even teams and one overloaded one from one even
# team and three overloaded ones, as long as the extremes match.
#
# The honest measure is the spread about the mean, and it is quadratic. It is
# written here the way it is meant:
#
#     minimize sum((load[t] - mean) * (load[t] - mean) for t in Teams)
#
# A product of two decisions is allowed in an objective and nowhere else. The
# compiler folds it into degree-two terms, decides whether the result is convex,
# and the engine is chosen from that: HiGHS minimises it directly as a convex
# quadratic when the model is continuous, and CP-SAT builds a variable per
# product when the model is discrete. Neither is asked to do the other's job.

problem balanced_workload "Balanced workload"
  "Spread a fixed body of work across teams so that no team carries a share "
  "far from the average, while respecting what each team can take."

set Teams = alpha, bravo, charlie, delta of team

param capacity[Teams] "Hours this team can take" = {
    alpha: 40, bravo: 40, charlie: 25, delta: 25 }

param minimum[Teams] default 0 "Hours this team is committed to regardless" = {
    alpha: 12, charlie: 5 }

param total_work "Hours to be shared out" = 96

# ------------------------------------------------------------- decisions

var load[Teams] continuous in [0, 40] means "Hours this team is given"

var mean_load continuous in [0, 40] means "Average hours across the teams"

# ------------------------------------------------------------ hard rules

constraint all_work_is_shared_out "Every hour of work is given to some team"
  category physical
  sum(load[t] for t in Teams) == total_work

constraint within_capacity "No team is given more than it can take"
  category physical
  forall t in Teams:
    load[t] <= capacity[t]

constraint standing_commitments_are_kept "A team already committed keeps its hours"
  category operational
  forall t in Teams where minimum[t] > 0:
    load[t] >= minimum[t]

constraint mean_is_the_average "The mean is the average of the loads"
  category modelling
  because "Stating it as a decision rather than a constant lets the spread be "
          "measured about the average the plan actually produces"
  4 * mean_load == sum(load[t] for t in Teams)

# -------------------------------------------------------------- objective

minimize imbalance "Spread of team loads about their mean"
  unit "hours squared":
  sum((load[t] - mean_load) * (load[t] - mean_load) for t in Teams)

# ------------------------------------------------------------ assumptions

assume balance_is_a_variance "Balance is the spread of loads about the mean, "
                             "not the gap between the extremes"
  because "A range cannot tell one overloaded team from three, so long as the "
          "busiest and idlest match; the spread can"
  affects imbalance, mean_is_the_average

assume work_is_divisible "Work can be split into any fraction of an hour"
  because "It is what keeps the model continuous, which is what lets the "
          "quadratic be solved directly rather than searched over"
  affects all_work_is_shared_out

# -------------------------------------------------------------- scenarios

scenario charlie_unavailable "Charlie's team is committed elsewhere"
  "Their capacity drops to what they are already committed to, so the same work "
  "has to be carried by three teams instead of four."
  set capacity[charlie] to 5

scenario more_work "A quarter more work, same teams"
  "Capacity starts to bind, and a perfectly even split stops being reachable."
  set total_work to 120
